# Cursor & Agent Rules - Lexi Project

# UI/UX Standards
- Always use ShadcnUI components.
- Maintain a premium, clean, and professional look.
- Use Tailwind CSS for all styling. No ad-hoc CSS unless necessary.
- Ensure all screens are mobile-responsive.

# Coding Standards
- Use TypeScript strictly. No `any` types.
- Follow Next.js 15+ App Router patterns (Server Components by default).
- Keep components small and reusable in `@/components` or `@/features`.
- Use `lucide-react` for icons.

# Project Specifics
- Project Name: Lexi
- Main Focus: AI English Speaking & Flashcards
- Backend: AWS SAM Serverless

# AI Behavior
- Be concise.
- Explain "Why" before "What" when assisting a Level C user. Use Vietnamese for explanations.
- **Docs First Policy:** Use `nextjs_docs` and `nextjs_index` BEFORE any code refactoring or feature implementation.
- Always check `AGENTS.md` before starting a new feature phase.
- Proactively run `pnpm dev` and check browser logs if needed to verify UI stability.
